Description: declarative tmux sessions with exact pane exit status
 A stateful wrapper around libtmux for building tmux sessions of named
 windows and panes, with exit status, exit events and stop escalation for
 the commands running in them.
 .
 Includes lte-run, a prefix command that supervises a command typed into a
 pane and reports its exact exit status to the session, and lte-key, which
 borrows a tmux prefix key for one session without editing ~/.tmux.conf.
